{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":43365664,"ns":0,"title":"Bagpipe theorem","extract":"In mathematics, the bagpipe theorem of Peter Nyikos describes the structure of the connected (but possibly non-paracompact) ω-bounded surfaces by showing that they are \"bagpipes\": the connected sum of a compact \"bag\" with several \"long pipes\".","description":"On structure of ω-bounded connected surfaces","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}